  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The cloud's billows, the flicker pattern, the bolt's path and forks, the rain and the marks vary per cast. The 0.82 s brew and the strike at 820 ms stay fixed: the cloud is the telegraph and the dodge window must be fair."
  },
  "director_notes": "A summoned thunderstorm, built to differ from the two existing sky strikes: Sky Strike is a quick single bolt with a leader, and Boss Storm Call telegraphs with a warning ring on the ground. Here the telegraph is the storm itself: (1) a dark cloud boils up over the target for 0.82 s and flickers from inside (a flickering glow and short arcs in the cloud), with the scene dimming and wind rising; (2) a massive forked bolt drops out of it with no leader, re-strikes twice, and the thunderclap (boom) comes 220 ms after the crack, like real thunder; (3) a cloudburst of rain (thin falling streaks out of the cloud) and wet ground marks follow, which no other lightning template has. Side is the hero for a side-on fighting game, where the cloud above and the tall bolt read best; the cloud sinks a little as it brews (negative rise) so it hangs in frame, and its puffs are scattered wide (spread_px, a new smoke param) so it reads as a cloud bank rather than a puff of smoke. The viewer's smoke is soft sprites, so the cloud is a cluster of dark puffs; the shader notes ask for a proper cloud."
}
